  "_ambiguous_comment": [
    "D4 trigger data. A phrase here legitimately maps to MORE THAN ONE",
    "covered service, so matching it means Daleel must ASK rather than guess.",
    "",
    "This is declared explicitly rather than inferred from overlapping",
    "variants, because an accidental keyword collision is not the same thing",
    "as a real citizen ambiguity, and only one of the two should stop and ask.",
    "",
    "'disambiguators' resolve the ambiguity WITHOUT asking. They are matched",
    "on WORD BOUNDARIES (unlike variants, which are matched as substrings so",
    "that Arabic attached prefixes still hit). That distinction matters:",
    "«جديد» must not match inside «تجديد».",
    "",
    "If exactly one option's disambiguators match -> resolve, do not ask.",
    "If zero or several match -> ask, using question_ar and the option labels",
    "as tappable buttons. No LLM call, so it fires identically every demo."
  ],

  "ambiguous_phrases": [
    {
      "_comment": [
        "REAL ambiguity, from the official ROP passport page. New issuance",
        "and renewal are different procedures on the SAME page: new issuance",
        "for an under-18 must be submitted by the guardian, renewal by the",
        "applicant themselves. «أريد جواز سفر» genuinely does not say which,",
        "and answering either one confidently would be wrong half the time."
      ],
